chx:Research a res:ResearchProject ; rdfs:label "Text-to-speech and speech recognition engines for an advanced course: chapter 24 and today's pyttsx3, Whisper, yt-dlp and the speech engines of Windows, macOS and Linux"@en ;
    sen0414:methodology "Primary source first: the chapter's named concepts from the textbook ontology built over the published chapter. Then the official documentation for the current release and the PEPs the chapter's topics touch. Every source opened and read on 2026-10-14T20:00:00; every claim taken from text actually read; every behaviour executed under Python 3.14.6." ;
    res:hasResearchScope chx:Scope ; rdfs:member chx:P01, chx:P02, chx:P03, chx:P04, chx:P05, chx:P06, chx:P07, chx:P08, chx:P09, chx:P10, chx:P11, chx:P12, chx:P13, chx:P14, chx:P15, chx:P16, chx:P17, chx:P18, chx:P19, chx:P20, chx:P21, chx:P22, chx:P23, chx:P24, chx:P25, chx:P26, chx:P27, chx:P28, chx:P29, chx:P30, chx:P31, chx:P32, chx:P33, chx:P34, chx:P35, chx:P36, chx:P37, chx:P38, chx:P39, chx:P40, chx:P41, chx:P42, chx:P43, chx:P44, chx:P45, chx:P46, chx:P47, chx:P48, chx:P49, chx:P50, chx:P51, chx:P52, chx:P53, chx:P54, chx:P55, chx:P56, chx:P57, chx:P58, chx:P59, chx:P60, chx:P61, chx:P62, chx:P63, chx:P64, chx:P65, chx:P66, chx:P67, chx:P68, chx:P69 .
chx:Scope a res:ResearchScope ; res:hasResearchQuestion "What does chapter 24 of the 3rd edition teach about speech from text with pyttsx3 (the engine, say and runAndWait, voices, rate and volume, WAV files), text from speech with Whisper (the models and Table 24-1, transcribe), subtitle files, downloading with yt-dlp and the practice programs, which of its 17 listings, printed outputs and statements still hold under Python 3.14.6 with pyttsx3 2.99, openai-whisper 20250625 and yt-dlp 2026.8.19, how do other Python, pyttsx3, Whisper and yt-dlp releases, the speech libraries of the three operating systems and the hardware of the machine change them, and what must an advanced course correct or add so that it matches the packages, the platforms and the files the book ships?" ; res:hasTimeWindow "Current as of 2026-10-14." .
